1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,040
Sponsorship and social media are a sensitive topic in our sport because you've probably noticed that many people jump for the camera.

2
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:17,440
There are a lot of people who do specific stunts or moves purely for social media.

3
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:22,460
Everyone wants to make a living from this sport, which is actually very difficult.

4
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:37,820
To make a living in this sport, you either have to be exceptionally good, be able to market yourself well, or simply get lucky with sponsorship deals.

5
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:47,820
Many people take huge risks just to become well known, gain lots of followers, and attract sponsorship deals because of those follower numbers.

6
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:52,420
Personally, social media has absolutely no value to me.

7
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:55,400
I'd actually be happy if I didn't have it.

8
00:00:56,120 --> 00:01:08,800
But I also know it's how I get my students, my sponsorship deals and ultimately my audience.

9
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:13,940
When you approach a sponsor, they don't ask how good you are. They ask how many followers you have.

10
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:16,120
And I think that's the sad part about this sport.

11
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:27,240
It's no longer about your actual ability. It's simply about your audience and how many views you've generated over the last 30 days.

12
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:35,360
I think that's really unfortunate because there are so many incredibly talented people

13
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:41,480
who'll find it very difficult to make a living simply because they don't have the audience.

14
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:50,220
People know who they are, a little under the radar, but on social media, nobody really knows them.

15
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,060
And I think that's a real shame.

16
00:01:53,620 --> 00:02:02,020
I also know that social media brings a lot of dangers because many people focus only on the camera.

17
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:03,740
They don't focus on the jump.

18
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:09,500
They're thinking: Is the camera set up correctly? Did I film the right line? I think that's really unfortunate.

